   "audience": "Owners",
   "title": "Homes sell for less than a year ago",
   "text": "From November 2025 to October 2026, Ontario homes sold for 6.8% less than similar homes in the same areas a year earlier. Condo apartments: −9.2%; detached houses: −5.6%. The drop is getting smaller: −8.2% in Q1 2026, −6.2% in Q3 2026."
  },
  {
   "id": "room",
   "audience": "Buyers",
   "title": "Buyers have room to negotiate",
   "text": "In the last 12 months, 76% of homes sold in the 15 cities in this report sold for less than their first asking price. Of the 27,933 homes for sale there now, 29% have cut their price."
  },
  {
   "id": "sales",
   "audience": "Sellers",
   "title": "More homes are selling",
   "text": "17,385 homes sold in the 15 cities in this report from August to October 2026, 14% more than in the same months a year earlier. The change ranged from +24% in Markham to −5% in Ajax."
  },
  {
   "id": "city_prices",
   "audience": "Sellers",
   "title": "The median price fell in 14 of 15 cities",
   "text": "From August to October 2026, the median sale price was lower than a year earlier in 14 of 15 cities. The largest drop was in Oshawa (−9.1%, to $635,000); Oakville rose 1.7%. Medians move with the mix of homes sold."
  },
  {
   "id": "power_of_sale",
   "audience": "Owners",
   "title": "More sales are power of sale",
   "text": "From August to October 2026, 158 of 36,125 Ontario home sales (0.44%) were power of sale, up from 0.29% a year earlier. That is still a small share of the market."
  }
